From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:24:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] network settings: the connected network's name ends in ...
 instead of being cut off

With the page-scroll arrows on, PageScrollController reserves their
52 px strip out of status_cards, the left column, which is only 40% of
the overlay. The SSID row's name label was content width and a flex row
never shrinks an item, so the row ran past its card and the end of the
name was cut off beside the arrows (AD5X, 800x480, Wi-Fi and Ethernet
both connected). The label now takes the free width (width 1, flex
grow, as pa_tuning_overlay's rows do) and ends in dots, so the signal
and forget icons stay in view. Kiln OS issue #4 came back this way.
---
 ui_xml/network_settings_overlay.xml | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui_xml/network_settings_overlay.xml b/ui_xml/network_settings_overlay.xml
index b1841cd169..7fba56ecb7 100644
--- a/ui_xml/network_settings_overlay.xml
+++ b/ui_xml/network_settings_overlay.xml
@@ -103,8 +103,11 @@
                         height="content" style_pad_all="0" scrollable="false" flex_flow="row"
                         style_flex_main_place="start" style_flex_cross_place="center" style_pad_gap="#space_xs">
                   <icon src="check_circle" size="sm" variant="success"/>
-                  <text_body name="ssid_label" bind_text="connected_ssid"/>
-                  <lv_obj height="1" flex_grow="1" scrollable="false"/>
+                  <!-- Takes the free width and ends in "...": a content-width name
+                       can't shrink in the row, so with the page-scroll arrows on
+                       (their strip comes out of this column) its end was cut off -->
+                  <text_body name="ssid_label" bind_text="connected_ssid"
+                             width="1" flex_grow="1" long_mode="dots"/>
                   <icon src="wifi_strength_4" size="sm" variant="primary"/>
                   <!-- Forget the currently connected network (with confirmation) -->
                   <icon name="forget_network_icon"
